## Code Structure and Style
- Always implement modular design with clear separation of concerns
- Use type hints for all function parameters and return values
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines strictly
- Implement proper error handling with custom exception classes
- Use dataclasses for data structures where appropriate

## Security Requirements
- Implement input validation for all user-provided data
- Use secure random number generation (secrets module) for any randomization
- Sanitize all file paths and implement proper file access controls
- Never execute raw user input as code
- Implement proper authentication and authorization checks

## Testing Standards
- Maintain minimum 90% test coverage
- Implement unit tests for all core functionality
- Include integration tests for system components
- Use property-based testing for data structures
- Implement performance benchmarks

## Documentation Requirements
- Include detailed docstrings for all classes and functions
- Maintain up-to-date API documentation
- Document all dependencies and their versions
- Include setup and deployment instructions
- Document security considerations and threat models

## Performance Optimization
- Implement caching for frequently accessed data
- Use asyncio for I/O-bound operations
- Implement proper memory management
- Profile code regularly for performance bottlenecks
- Use appropriate data structures for operations

## Code Quality
- Maintain cyclomatic complexity below 10
- Keep functions focused and under 50 lines
- Implement proper logging with different log levels
- Use type checkers (mypy) in strict mode
- Run linters (pylint, flake8) with strict settings

## Version Control
- Use semantic versioning
- Write descriptive commit messages
- Maintain a clean git history
- Tag all releases
- Document breaking changes

## AI-Specific Rules
- Implement bias detection and mitigation
- Include model versioning and tracking
- Document model limitations and assumptions
- Implement fallback mechanisms
- Monitor and log AI decisions